    <p>I build products at the seam where traditional financial markets and crypto infrastructure have to meet &mdash; the ones that decide what a position costs to hold, when it gets unwound, and who is exposed when it does, all inside the perimeters regulators draw. I build regulated financial products for retail users on Coinbase Advanced and institutional clients on Coinbase Prime, powered by the exchanges underneath. Building products is what I do first and foremost; deep risk and derivatives is the domain I do it in.</p>
    <p>I'm a Product Manager at <a href="https://www.coinbase.com/blog/coinbase-brings-global-crypto-derivatives-to-us-market" rel="noopener">Coinbase Financial Markets</a>, our US-regulated FCM, which this year became the first to connect US clients to global crypto derivatives. I joined Coinbase in 2021 pre-IPO as the 4th hire on the Credit Risk team, then built and shipped the core infrastructure behind <a href="https://www.coinbase.com/international-exchange" rel="noopener">Coinbase International Exchange</a> and our FCM &mdash; the margin engine, the auto-liquidation waterfall, the position limits &mdash; work that gave me the domain depth I now bring to product. Before crypto, I underwrote counterparty risk at Morgan Stanley and J.P. Morgan.</p>
    <p>My first product was Retail Borrow, bitcoin-backed loans for US retail customers, where I built the risk and liquidation framework. Everything since has been a version of the same question at larger size: who is exposed when the collateral moves, and how gently can you unwind them.</p>
    <p>I have an MBA from NYU Stern, earned while working full time, and I spend most of my time on the tail — risk products are judged on the worst hour of the worst week, not the median.</p>
