          <h3>Coinbase Financial Markets, the US derivatives FCM</h3>
          <p>I built the US derivatives FCM from zero on the risk side, standing up the framework a CFTC-regulated venue needs before it can take a trade. I'm now on the product team bringing global derivatives liquidity to the US customer base.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="slide" data-g="exchanges">
        <div class="slide-fig"><b>First</b></div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <div class="meta"><span class="pill">May 2026</span><span class="pill">Coinbase Financial Markets</span></div>
          <h3>Global derivatives, opened to US customers</h3>
          <p>Derivatives are roughly 80% of global crypto trading volume, and until this year US clients had no regulated way in — some institutions stood up offshore entities just to get there. Coinbase Financial Markets became the first and only US-regulated FCM connecting US clients to global perps and options.</p>
          <p class="mine">I helped develop the risk framework behind Coinbase Financial Markets&rsquo; CFTC/NFA application, and built OTC options for US customers on Coinbase Prime plugged into Deribit&rsquo;s global liquidity &mdash; the piece that let US clients reach that book at all.</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://www.coinbase.com/blog/coinbase-brings-global-crypto-derivatives-to-us-market" rel="noopener">Read the announcement ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="slide" data-g="exchanges">
        <div class="slide-fig"><b>0&rarr;1</b></div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <div class="meta"><span class="pill">2023</span><span class="pill">Founding team</span></div>
          <h3>Coinbase International Exchange</h3>
          <p>Built from scratch as a regulated, institutional-grade offshore derivatives exchange &mdash; now processing $333B+ in 30-day trading volume, with $42B+ of open interest across 145 listed assets.</p>
          <p class="mine">I joined before it launched and helped build the infrastructure from the ground up &mdash; the core exchange systems and risk framework: auto-liquidation engine, margin models, capital efficiency features, and the governance infrastructure that manages exposure across our client base. Years later, that same infrastructure supports billions in trading volume and is a foundational part of Coinbase&rsquo;s derivatives offering.</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://www.coinbase.com/international-exchange" rel="noopener">See the exchange ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="slide" data-g="exchanges">
        <div class="slide-fig"><b>$2.9B</b></div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <div class="meta"><span class="pill">Closed Aug 2025</span><span class="pill">Largest deal in crypto</span></div>
          <h3>Deribit joins Coinbase</h3>
          <p>Deribit traded over $1 trillion in 2024 and holds roughly $60B of open interest. Merging it with our international venue meant reconciling two live books — two risk models, two margin methodologies — without interrupting either.</p>
          <p class="mine">[Your part — which side of the merge you owned.]</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://www.coinbase.com/blog/deribit-joins-coinbase-unlocking-the-future-of-global-crypto-derivatives" rel="noopener">Read the announcement ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="slide" data-g="exchanges">
        <div class="slide-fig"><b>$13B</b></div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <div class="meta"><span class="pill">2020</span><span class="pill">Morgan Stanley</span></div>
          <h3>E*TRADE integration</h3>
          <p>The largest US bank deal since the financial crisis, closed October 2020 — folding a 38-year-old direct-to-consumer brokerage into an advisor-led wealth franchise then overseeing $3.3 trillion. Two firms with different clients, risk appetites and systems of record had to become one.</p>
          <p class="mine">I worked the integration directly with the Managing Director and Head of Credit Risk, and was top underwriter across the combined $100B+ margin book &mdash; specialising in clients carrying $50M+ in credit exposure.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="slide" data-g="systems">
        <div class="slide-fig"><b>1st</b></div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <div class="meta"><span class="pill">2021</span><span class="pill">First product</span></div>
          <h3>Retail Borrow</h3>
          <p>Bitcoin-backed cash loans for US retail customers. I built the risk and liquidation framework and managed the product — the same mechanics as liquidating a trader, with none of the same tolerance for getting it wrong.</p>
          <p class="mine">[Your part — where you set LTV thresholds and how much warning a borrower got.]</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="slide" data-g="systems">
        <div class="slide-fig"><b>200+</b></div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <div class="meta"><span class="pill">2023</span><span class="pill">Risk</span></div>
          <h3>The risk framework</h3>
          <p>The rulebook a regulated venue launches on: margin tiers, position limits, trade controls, and the conditions under which the exchange stops accepting a trade.</p>
          <p class="mine">[Your part — the tradeoff you argued for, and who you had to convince.]</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="slide" data-g="systems">
        <div class="slide-fig"><b>24/7</b></div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <div class="meta"><span class="pill">2024</span><span class="pill">Product</span></div>
          <h3>The auto-liquidation engine</h3>
          <p>How a position unwinds when margin runs out — fast enough that one failing account never reaches the insurance fund, let alone the rest of the book. Unwind too slowly and the loss outruns the collateral; too fast and you move the market against everyone.</p>
          <p class="mine">I built the auto-liquidation engine, the automated liquidation waterfall, and the market-making backstop liquidity program behind it &mdash; the layered defence that keeps one failing account from reaching the fund.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="slide" data-g="systems">
        <div class="slide-fig"><b>40+</b></div>
        <div class="slide-body">
          <div class="meta"><span class="pill">2024 &ndash; 2025</span><span class="pill">Product</span></div>
          <h3>Margin models</h3>
          <p>What a position costs to hold across perps, dated futures, options and spot — and how much correlated risk the venue will let a trader net against it. Clients can post cross-collateral across 40+ assets against a single balance.</p>
          <p class="mine">[Your part — the stress case where you refused to net.]</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://www.coinbase.com/international-exchange" rel="noopener">Margin and collateral ↗</a>
        </div>
